\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces 16\,nm, one downward sweep. Top: reading of the taps whose failure boundary falls inside the sweep, in placement A (solid) and in the same routed design with the 250\,ps guard of Section~\ref {sec:guard} (dashed); a point is drawn while the tap's checker saw no error. Bottom: error rate of the failing points of placement A (fraction of cycles in which FF2 held the wrong value).}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:shmoo}{{2}{3}{16\,nm, one downward sweep. Top: reading of the taps whose failure boundary falls inside the sweep, in placement A (solid) and in the same routed design with the 250\,ps guard of Section~\ref {sec:guard} (dashed); a point is drawn while the tap's checker saw no error. Bottom: error rate of the failing points of placement A (fraction of cycles in which FF2 held the wrong value)}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Measured margin $m$ at failure versus the offset $\Delta ^{*}_\mathrm  {STA}$ predicted by STA without the uncertainty and pessimism terms (slow corner). Filled: the independent failing taps of the two placements; hollow: the same routed taps with a guard band ($\Delta ^{*}_\mathrm  {STA}$ from the STA of the guarded design). Error bars span the 10\,mV interval in which errors start. Below zero the path fails while the sensor still reads positive.}}{3}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:offset}{{3}{3}{Measured margin $m$ at failure versus the offset $\Dst $ predicted by STA without the uncertainty and pessimism terms (slow corner). Filled: the independent failing taps of the two placements; hollow: the same routed taps with a guard band ($\Dst $ from the STA of the guarded design). Error bars span the 10\,mV interval in which errors start. Below zero the path fails while the sensor still reads positive}{figure.3}{}}
